 "manufacturer": "MDD (Microdiode Semiconductor)",
 "title": "20 V N-channel enhancement MOSFET in SOT-23",
 "source": {
  "revision": "V1.1",
  "pages": 6
 },
 "summary": "A single N-channel enhancement-mode MOSFET made on a trench process, in the three-lead SOT-23. It blocks 20 V, takes ±12 V on the gate and carries 4 A continuously at 25 °C ambient, 12 A pulsed. On-resistance is 25 mΩ typical, 30 mΩ max with 4.5 V on the gate, and 28 mΩ typical, 35 mΩ max at 2.5 V; the threshold lies between 0.5 V and 1.2 V. Uses named for it are load switches, general switching, high-speed line drivers and power management.",
