   "fixture": true,
   "description": "The fixture for the switching times. A pulse generator Vgs drives the gate through Rgen; the drain is loaded by Rl to the Vdd supply and the source goes to ground. The gate voltage is observed as Vin and the drain voltage as Vout. The switching rows are taken with VDS = 10 V, VGS = 4.5 V, ID = 3 A, RG = 6 Ω and RL = 5.5 Ω. Read on the waveforms of Figure 2, with Vout inverted: td(on) runs from the input crossing 10 % on its rise to the output reaching 10 % of its swing, tr from 10 % to 90 % of the output swing, and ton is their sum; td(off) runs from the input falling through 90 % to the output returning to 90 %, tf from 90 % back to 10 %, and toff is their sum. The input pulse width is taken between its 50 % points.",
