 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The channel starts to conduct at 0.5 to 1.2 V on the gate (0.8 V typical, 250 µA). On-resistance is specified at two drive levels: 30 mΩ max at 4.5 V and 4 A, 35 mΩ max at 2.5 V and 3 A. The gate is rated ±12 V, and its leakage stays under ±100 nA at ±10 V. Figure 9 shows on-resistance at 2.9 A climbing steeply as the gate falls toward 2 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With 10 V across it, 4.5 V on the gate, 3 A, a 6 Ω gate resistor and a 5.5 Ω load, the part turns on in 12 ns delay plus 36 ns rise and off in 34 ns delay plus 10 ns fall, typical. A full swing to 4.5 V takes 5.4 nC of gate charge, of which 0.65 nC is gate-source and 1.6 nC gate-drain; in Figure 11 the Miller plateau sits near 1.5 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "On-resistance at 4.5 V drive rises roughly linearly with junction temperature, to about 1.55 times its 25 °C value at 150 °C (Figure 8). Figure 3 derates dissipation from 1 W at 25 °C to zero at 140 °C; Figure 4 shows drain current falling from about 3 A at 25 °C to about 0.3 A at 140 °C. In Figure 7 the 125 °C transfer curve conducts at a lower gate voltage than the 25 °C curve."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 1.25 W dissipation and 100 °C/W junction-to-ambient figures assume a 1 in² double-sided FR-4 board with 2 oz copper in still air at 25 °C. The junction and storage range is -50 °C to 150 °C. Figure 14 gives the transient thermal impedance for repeated and single pulses, and Figure 13 the single-pulse safe operating area at 25 °C ambient, bounded by on-resistance at low voltage and by the 20 V breakdown on the right."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-to-drain body diode carries at most 1.6 A at 25 °C and drops at most 1.2 V at 1 A with the gate at 0 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "SOT-23: pin 1 gate and pin 2 source on one long side, pin 3 drain alone on the other. Outline dimensions are in millimetres; the land pattern is given in inches and millimetres; the general tolerance is ±0.05 mm. The top face carries S2 and a date code."
  }
 ],
